`the tables of sganim-rishonim-kayamim` MEANS
    LIST `annex א'19 of 1.9.2016`, `annex א'20 of 1.9.2016`, `annex א'21 of 1.9.2016`, `annex א'22 of 1.9.2016`

`the 2015 annexes of sganim-rishonim-kayamim` MEANS
    LIST `annex יב of 2015`, `annex יג of 2015`, `annex יד of 2015`, `annex טו of 2015`

§§ `בדיקת הטבלאות`

-- (1) The rows: the complexity levels the 2015 table prints (levels 2 to 8), the
-- grades א to ד with the intermediate א+, ב+ and ג+.
#ASSERT and (zipWith (GIVEN t, a YIELD `the published labels of` t EQUALS catMaybes (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row label`) (`the rows of the 2015 annex` a)))
                     `the tables of sganim-rishonim-kayamim` `the 2015 annexes of sganim-rishonim-kayamim`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD t's `published table from` EQUALS `the managers' tables of sganim-rishonim-kayamim are updated from`) `the tables of sganim-rishonim-kayamim`

-- (2) The 2015 tables raised to 1.1.2015: each cell taken back by the rise
-- of 1.1.2015 over the third part's tables (1.0635/1.0575, as the tables of
-- 1.1.2015 rise) is the 2015 table's cell to the nearest shekel
-- (convention rounding.half). A check sets the 2015 cell beside the cell
-- here taken back and rounded.
GIVEN t IS A `published table`, a IS A `2015 salary annex`
GIVETH A LIST OF `published cell check`
DECIDE `the cells of sganim-rishonim-kayamim taken back to 2015 beside` t a IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD
                     concat (map (GIVEN c YIELD
                                      CONSIDER `the 2015 table pay` a (r's `published row label`) (c's grade)
                                      WHEN JUST old THEN LIST (`a published check` (r's `published row label`) (c's grade) old
                                                                   (`to the nearest whole` (c's pay DIVIDED BY `the rise of 1.1.2015 over the third part's tables`)))
                                      WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY)
                                 (r's `published row cells`)))
                (t's `published table rows`))

`the 2015 checks of sganim-rishonim-kayamim` MEANS
    concat (zipWith `the cells of sganim-rishonim-kayamim taken back to 2015 beside` `the tables of sganim-rishonim-kayamim` `the 2015 annexes of sganim-rishonim-kayamim`)

#ASSERT count `the 2015 checks of sganim-rishonim-kayamim` EQUALS sum (map `the published cell count of` `the tables of sganim-rishonim-kayamim`)
#ASSERT null (`the published misses in` `the 2015 checks of sganim-rishonim-kayamim`)

-- (3) Every table rises along its grades and down its levels, so "the
-- grade nearest at or above" (§71(ב)) is one cell.
#ASSERT all `the published table rises along its grades and down its rows` `the tables of sganim-rishonim-kayamim`

-- The tables at work.
#ASSERT `the published table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) `annex א'19 of 1.9.2016` 2 1 EQUALS JUST 11359.35
